From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your Name <you@example.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bus off detection and error counters in FlexCANDevice

`getBusOffState()`, `getRxErrorCounter()` and `getTxErrorCounter()` used
the setter macros of the device header to read status fields. The macros
shift their argument into the field instead of extracting it
(`FLEXCAN_ESR1_FLTCONF(x)` is `((x << 4) & 0x30)`), so the code
evaluated the wrong bits:

- `getBusOffState()` looked at ESR1 bits 1..0 (ERRINT and bit 0, which
  the device header leaves undefined) instead
  of the fault confinement field in bits 4..5. ERRINT is set by any
  error frame, so the first error frame put the driver into BUS_OFF, and
  since `fBusOff` is sticky it stayed there until the device was
  restarted or a frame was received. A controller that really went bus
  off (ESR1[FLTCONF] = 1x, no interrupt flag set) was not detected at
  all. On a running bus we measured ESR1 = 0x00240082 (ERRINT and IDLE
  set, FLTCONF = 0, TEC/REC 30/0) and the driver reported BUS_OFF.
- `getRxErrorCounter()` returned `(ECR << 8) & 0xFF00` truncated to
  uint8_t, which is always 0.
- `getTxErrorCounter()` worked by accident, because TXERRCNT starts at
  bit 0, but read the whole register instead of the field.

All three now extract the field with mask and shift.

The new host test `FlexCANDeviceTest` covers the four fault confinement
states and the error counters. `bspFlexCan` is not part of the unit test
build, so the test brings a test-only `mcu/mcu.h` with the FlexCAN
register layout and provides host memory at the base address of
FlexCAN_0, which `FlexCANDevice` uses to derive its instance index.

Signed-off-by: Your Name <you@example.com>
---
 CMakeLists.txt                                     |   1 +
 .../bsp/bspFlexCan/include/can/FlexCANDevice.h     |  16 ++-
 .../s32k1xx/bsp/bspFlexCan/test/CMakeLists.txt     |  20 +++
 .../s32k1xx/bsp/bspFlexCan/test/include/mcu/mcu.h  |  19 +++
 .../bspFlexCan/test/src/can/FlexCANDeviceTest.cpp  | 159 +++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 212 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 1dc44b64..c69a5d3e 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -216,6 +216,7 @@ if (BUILD_EXECUTABLE STREQUAL "unitTest")
 
         add_subdirectory(platforms/s32k1xx/bsp/bspCore/test)
         add_subdirectory(platforms/s32k1xx/bsp/bspEepromDriver/test)
+        add_subdirectory(platforms/s32k1xx/bsp/bspFlexCan/test)
         add_subdirectory(platforms/s32k1xx/bsp/bspIo/test)
         add_subdirectory(platforms/s32k1xx/bsp/canflex2Transceiver/test)
         add_subdirectory(platforms/s32k1xx/bsp/bspUart/test)
diff --git a/platforms/s32k1xx/bsp/bspFlexCan/include/can/FlexCANDevice.h b/platforms/s32k1xx/bsp/bspFlexCan/include/can/FlexCANDevice.h
index d760ad92..f646cfdb 100644
--- a/platforms/s32k1xx/bsp/bspFlexCan/include/can/FlexCANDevice.h
+++ b/platforms/s32k1xx/bsp/bspFlexCan/include/can/FlexCANDevice.h
@@ -179,12 +179,20 @@ public:
     /**
      * \return the number of Transmit errors
      */
-    uint8_t getTxErrorCounter() { return FLEXCAN_ECR_TXERRCNT(fpDevice->ECR); }
+    uint8_t getTxErrorCounter()
+    {
+        return static_cast<uint8_t>(
+            (fpDevice->ECR & FLEXCAN_ECR_TXERRCNT_MASK) >> FLEXCAN_ECR_TXERRCNT_SHIFT);
+    }
 
     /**
      * \return the number of Receive errors
      */
-    uint8_t getRxErrorCounter() { return FLEXCAN_ECR_RXERRCNT(fpDevice->ECR); }
+    uint8_t getRxErrorCounter()
+    {
+        return static_cast<uint8_t>(
+            (fpDevice->ECR & FLEXCAN_ECR_RXERRCNT_MASK) >> FLEXCAN_ECR_RXERRCNT_SHIFT);
+    }
 
     /**
      * \return the off status of the bus
@@ -196,7 +204,9 @@ public:
         // FLTCONF: 00 error active
         //          01 error passive
         //          1X bus off
-        if ((FLEXCAN_ESR1_FLTCONF(fpDevice->ESR1) > 1) || fBusOff)
+        uint32_t const faultConfinement
+            = (fpDevice->ESR1 & FLEXCAN_ESR1_FLTCONF_MASK) >> FLEXCAN_ESR1_FLTCONF_SHIFT;
+        if ((faultConfinement > 1U) || fBusOff)
         {
             fBusOff = true;
             return BUS_OFF;
diff --git a/platforms/s32k1xx/bsp/bspFlexCan/test/CMakeLists.txt b/platforms/s32k1xx/bsp/bspFlexCan/test/CMakeLists.txt
